{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1334170-spun-or-unspun-the-paradox-of-time-travel","id":1334170,"title":"Spun or unspun? The paradox of time travel.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-09-06T08:14:43-07:00","id":1334170,"title":"Spun or unspun? The paradox of time travel.","content":"It\u2019s currently t=0, and you notice that a fellow Mage is back in time from t=10. To you, t=0 is the present and t=(0,10] is unwritten/not \u201cspun.\u201d To them, t=10 is the present and t=[0,10] is spun. What do?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-06T08:30:28-07:00","id":1334174,"title":"","content":"If you\u2019re seeing a Mage with a Time aura you are not in the Present.<br /> <br /> Interestingly, things or people the time traveler interacts with (and I assume interaction can be as casual as being observed) also pick up a Time aura and thus become capable of also changing the Present if they have the means to know they\u2019ve been afforded this opportunity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-13T05:49:55-07:00","id":1335475,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1334170-spun-or-unspun-the-paradox-of-time-travel?p=1334174#post1334174\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you\u2019re seeing a Mage with a Time aura you are not in the Present.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then there <i>is</i> no present or future, only past, because more likely than not someone somewhere is Shifting Sands-ing at any given point in time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-13T06:41:01-07:00","id":1335484,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1334170-spun-or-unspun-the-paradox-of-time-travel?p=1335475#post1335475\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then there <i>is</i> no present or future, only past, because more likely than not someone somewhere is Shifting Sands-ing at any given point in time.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is immaterial, because the metaphysics of time travel in Mage are explicitly &quot;there is an objective 'present' that time travelers catch back up to after they make the jump&quot; and the only things time travel affects are things that time travelers actually affect within the span of their travel.<br /> <br /> It doesn't matter one whit to the London chapter of the Eleventh Question if some unrelated Acanthus in Osaka is scratching the record back thirty seconds, because the things they are likely to affect in that thirty seconds aren't going to interface with anything they do until much much later, if at all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-13T06:42:34-07:00","id":1335485,"title":"","content":"IMO, it honestly depends on the story. Are you supposed to stop this future person? Are they there to offer cryptic &quot;Ghost-of-Christmas-Yet-to-Come&quot; advice before disappearing? <br /> <br /> In any case, mechanically, though, this seems like exactly what the &quot;Aponoia&quot; Persistent Condition from Signs of Sorcery is meant to cover.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/518-alieron","name":"Alieron","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-13T12:17:15-07:00","id":1335574,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1334170-spun-or-unspun-the-paradox-of-time-travel?p=1335475#post1335475\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then there <i>is</i> no present or future, only past, because more likely than not someone somewhere is Shifting Sands-ing at any given point in time.</div> </div> </div> </div>Patently false as evidenced by the fact that things keep happening and things keep having a potential to happen.<br /> <br /> The Present is frozen for travelers, which is one of the ways they know that there is a Present they come from. The Future is uncertain which is how they know the Present keeps marching forward.<br /> <br /> Time travel is also effectively instantaneous to everyone except the traveler. To everyone except the traveler time keeps marching on. You\u2019ve gotten caught in the same fallacy as someone who said, \u201cOh no, if I give extra time to this rock I can end the world!\u201d<br /> <br /> Namely, you\u2019re conflating the traveler\u2019s subjective experience as overriding everyone else\u2019s. This isn\u2019t a thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 09-13-2019, 03:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-19T19:28:54-07:00","id":1390155,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1334170-spun-or-unspun-the-paradox-of-time-travel?p=1334174#post1334174\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you\u2019re seeing a Mage with a Time aura you are not in the Present.<br /> <br /> Interestingly, things or people the time traveler interacts with (and I assume interaction can be as casual as being observed) also pick up a Time aura and thus become capable of also changing the Present if they have the means to know they\u2019ve been afforded this opportunity.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know, I reviewed the source and it was ambiguous on whether the time aura shows up in the past, present, or both. I looked to the spells for clarifying context and their implications are not confirmations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26112-excess","name":"Excess","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-19T19:37:38-07:00","id":1390156,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1334170-spun-or-unspun-the-paradox-of-time-travel?p=1335484#post1335484\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which is immaterial, because the metaphysics of time travel in Mage are explicitly &amp;quot;there is an objective 'present' that time travelers catch back up to after they make the jump&amp;quot; and the only things time travel affects are things that time travelers actually affect within the span of their travel.<br /> <br /> It doesn't matter one whit to the London chapter of the Eleventh Question if some unrelated Acanthus in Osaka is scratching the record back thirty seconds, because the things they are likely to affect in that thirty seconds aren't going to interface with anything they do until much much later, if at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>An objective present? Not if Mummy: the curse 2nd edition has anything to say about it. The presentation for the Time arcanum even says nothing is eternal, yet this is contradicted by the existence of the Deceived. Maybe the Fall could be blamed for this? Is it a coincidence that so many supernatural cultures talk about a primordial time ended by something disastrous?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26112-excess","name":"Excess","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-19T19:57:11-07:00","id":1390161,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Excess</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1334170-spun-or-unspun-the-paradox-of-time-travel?p=1390155#post1390155\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know, I reviewed the source and it was ambiguous on whether the time aura shows up in the past, present, or both. I looked to the spells for clarifying context and their implications are not confirmations.</div> </div> </div> </div>The time aura showing up in &quot;the present,&quot; if it happens at all, means the spell's effect is at the very end of its possible runtime. That's how &quot;the spell moves you into the past and ends when its Duration runs out or you catch up to the present&quot; works.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Excess</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1334170-spun-or-unspun-the-paradox-of-time-travel?p=1390156#post1390156\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">An objective present? Not if Mummy: the curse 2nd edition has anything to say about it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Boy, is my face red. If only I had had the foresight to include qualifying elements of that sentence like &quot;the metaphysics of time travel in Mage.&quot; If only Mummy: the Curse 2e specified that the Arisen experience of time is <i>extremely weird</i>. Alas, I must make my peace with having said a thing about how time-magic works for mages in Mage that is different than how time-magic works on mummies in Mummy. Egg on my face, really.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-19T20:15:25-07:00","id":1390164,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Excess</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1334170-spun-or-unspun-the-paradox-of-time-travel?p=1390156#post1390156\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not if Mummy: the curse 2nd edition has anything to say about it.</div> </div> </div> </div>You do realize that inherently is Mummy: the Curse 2nd Edition's own shit storm to figure and has no bearing on how Mage (2nd, not about to bother with 1st) gives a shit about it's own temporal mechanics, yes?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-19T20:19:42-07:00","id":1390165,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1334170-spun-or-unspun-the-paradox-of-time-travel?p=1390164#post1390164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You do realize that inherently is Mummy: the Curse 2nd Edition's own shit storm to figure and has no bearing on how Mage (2nd, not about to bother with 1st) gives a shit about it's own temporal mechanics, yes?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, I disagree. That they even provide mechanics for how the Time arcanum interacts with the Arisen shows that they really do share a common setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26112-excess","name":"Excess","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-19T20:35:39-07:00","id":1390171,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Excess</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1334170-spun-or-unspun-the-paradox-of-time-travel?p=1390165#post1390165\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, I disagree. That they even provide mechanics for how the Time arcanum interacts with the Arisen shows that they really do share a common setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. They share a setting. A setting in which the Arisen <i>specifically do not interact with time in the normal fashion.</i> Where they are directly called out in their own game as having a unique relation to the flow of time multiple times within the text.<br /> <br /> You can disagree all you like, but an explicit exception doesn't invalidate the rule.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-19T20:55:11-07:00","id":1390177,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1334170-spun-or-unspun-the-paradox-of-time-travel?p=1390171#post1390171\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes. They share a setting. A setting in which the Arisen <i>specifically do not interact with time in the normal fashion.</i> Where they are directly called out in their own game as having a unique relation to the flow of time multiple times within the text.<br /> <br /> You can disagree all you like, but an explicit exception doesn't invalidate the rule.</div> </div> </div> </div>Depending on the context, yes it does. The Time arcanum deals with an objective present, which the Arisan shows is false. Not just that, but the paradoxes they interact with are not the exception but the rule. I have read those sections, the stability of time is an illusion. Chaos is the norm. Time is riddled with contradictions and with many of them being indistinguishable from deja-vu and schedule errors. We are so defined by time that we fail to see how incoherent it is. The Arisen are stable points in all of this. There is an implication that their temporal hijinks come from being the only ones exempt from this. Like being sane in the world of the insane.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26112-excess","name":"Excess","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-19T21:11:16-07:00","id":1390182,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Excess</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1334170-spun-or-unspun-the-paradox-of-time-travel?p=1390177#post1390177\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Depending on the context, yes it does. The Time arcanum deals with an objective present, which the Arisan shows is false. Not just that, but the paradoxes they interact with are not the exception but the rule. I have read those sections, the stability of time is an illusion. Chaos is the norm. Time is riddled with contradictions and with many of them being indistinguishable from deja-vu and schedule errors. We are so defined by time that we fail to see how incoherent it is. The Arisen are stable points in all of this. There is an implication that their temporal hijinks come from being the only ones exempt from this. Like being sane in the world of the insane.</div> </div> </div> </div>Excess, look at the forum this thread is posted in and tell me what gameline you think is most directly relevant to a question about mages doing time travel posed two months before the Mummy 2e KS started.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-19T21:24:25-07:00","id":1390186,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1334170-spun-or-unspun-the-paradox-of-time-travel?p=1390182#post1390182\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Excess, look at the forum this thread is posted in and tell me what gameline you think is most directly relevant to a question about mages doing time travel posed two months before the Mummy 2e KS started.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is related. We were discussing how time works and I brought it up organically as the settings overlapped. At this point you are sounding increasingly petty. What is going on?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26112-excess","name":"Excess","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-19T22:09:21-07:00","id":1390195,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Excess</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1334170-spun-or-unspun-the-paradox-of-time-travel?p=1390186#post1390186\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is related. We were discussing how time works and I brought it up organically as the settings overlapped. At this point you are sounding increasingly petty. What is going on?</div> </div> </div> </div>What's going on is that I got a post notification from a thread that began and ended eight months ago because you apparently wanted to gotcha me with information that did not exist publicly during that span of time and concerned a separate gameline that specifically says that it's a weird exception to how the vast majority of creatures deal with time.<br /> <br /> &quot;Time travel as typically experienced in Mage 2e through Time spells works the way described at the start of that Arcanum's section in the corebook,&quot; as an answer to a question about time travel posted well before November 2019 in the Mage: the Awakening subforum isn't meaningfully contradicted by &quot;the Arisen, who are the product of an impossibly powerful magical act that broke their origin point's relation to time, wake from deathly slumber intermittently and go through individual periods of activity like other beings with humanlike perception in an order that is not always chronologically linear, and this is repeatedly highlighted as unusual within the text of their own corebook manuscript, which was previewed in November 2019.&quot;<br /> <br /> The question is not about the nature of time in general in the Chronicles of Darkness. It's a question about how time travel works in Mage: the Awakening, a game which has defined rules for time travel \u2014 including explicit exceptions within Mage: the Awakening courtesy of Signs of Sorcery's material on Transportive Awakenings, which still works the same way as regular time travel except for moving where the objective present is for the purposes of Time spells used in the chronicle in which a displaced Acanthus operates.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-19T22:13:35-07:00","id":1390196,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Excess</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1334170-spun-or-unspun-the-paradox-of-time-travel?p=1390186#post1390186\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is related. We were discussing how time works and I brought it up organically as the settings overlapped. At this point you are sounding increasingly petty. What is going on?</div> </div> </div> </div>What is going on, from the outside, is someone who has a demonstrable newness to the material is arguing both against the relevant newness of the material which is Mummy 2e(less than a year old) vs Mage 2nd, which was released in 2016(2015? I forget the specifics), and has, both in the final manuscript and it's follow-up supplement (2019), asserted that the way other games operate and understood their metaphysics <i>has no fucking bearing on how Mage understands it's own sense of metaphysics, and, in fact, that disparity of understanding is the fucking drive of Mage's Arcana Experience System and Mage's systems as a whole, <u>wherein Mage's work to approximate the systems of other metaphysics into the bottomless gut of their own hunger-</u></i><br /> <br /> Sorry, lost myself there-<br /> <br /> My point is that someone who has demonstrated a minimal level of experience making what is newbie level mistakes against an argument with the level of material presented, both in text and out of text, is lacking.<br /> <br /> Make up for the lack if you want people to listen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-19T23:08:16-07:00","id":1390208,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Excess</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1334170-spun-or-unspun-the-paradox-of-time-travel?p=1390186#post1390186\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is related. We were discussing how time works and I brought it up organically as the settings overlapped. At this point you are sounding increasingly petty. What is going on?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, you necroposted on a thread that was about two-thirds of a year old and argued against points made where the material you're referencing didn't exist. To be fair, both Satchel and Arcane overreacted a bit. They have a reputation for being lore experts on these forums and don't like being contradicted. But, it's not like they were unprovoked.<br /> <br /> Thing about the CoD gamelines is that they're all designed to be their own games first; to stand on their own two feet with no other gameline supporting them. Also, CoD in general is like Burger King: you can have it your way. If you're just playing Mage and don't wanna involve any continuity from Mummy, go ahead. If you do, more power to you. Nothing's really set in stone, both in lore and mechanics (even if some people on here would have you believe otherwise). The corebooks simply give you a base and toolkit to work with.<br /> <br /> My personal take on Mage time mechanics is that time in not a wheel spinning threads, but rather a river. Like a river, Time flows in one direction, but the whole span of Time exists all at once. When a mage casts something like Shifting Sands, they pop out of the stream for a bit and thread to a previous point on the river and then dive back in. But keep in mind, this is just how I personally see it and play it. If I'm in someone else's game and they play it how the corebook does it, then I either play it that way or I simply leave the game.<br /> <br /> Please don't let this little experience drive you away from these forums. It's actually quite good here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","name":"crapcarp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-25T14:57:10-07:00","id":1391559,"title":"","content":"Reading this thread made me want to look over what the main book says about how time works, and how definitively it's presented. Mage 2nd edition does say on p. 186 that &quot;The Fallen World has the point at which the future becomes the past, which constantly advances.&quot; But I think you can argue that there's a slight amount of wiggle room in terms of whether to take this as the gospel truth, since p. 185 says &quot;Mages who study the Time Arcanum have practical experience to marry to Sleeping theory, and quickly discover that while some thinkers have approached something like the truth, thought experiments don\u2019t fully prepare them for the reality of temporal magic.&quot; You could read this as saying that mages have <i>inferred</i> the idea of an objective present from how they observe various time spells to work.<br /> <br /> So, if you don't like the idea of an objective present, and you can come up with an alternative metaphysics of time that fits with the facts derived from mages' &quot;practical experience&quot;, I think that isn't fundamentally changing the setting. The observations I see that seem to support the notion of a single objective present would be these ones from p. 185-186 (if anyone can think of any others let me know):<br /> <br /> 1. A mage who repeatedly looks into the future or past will find a given set of past event happens the same way each time since the past is already &quot;spun&quot;, while the future seem to be in flux because you may see multiple possible futures on different occasions when performing the same spell repeatedly (or in some cases a single spell like Choose the Thread may allow the mage to see multiple possible futures).<br /> <br /> 2. Mages who actually travel back in time with the Corridors of Time spell will have a &quot;telltale temporal aura&quot;, as will anything they interact with to change its destiny, but this aura will disappear when they return to the present.<br /> <br /> 3. &quot;Mages who travel back in time and look forward find that the intervening span is still set&quot;--so even if you are changing things in the past, it's as if you're just changing things in a new &quot;draft&quot; of history but when you look ahead you'll still see the original version of history prior to the present you departed from, with the altered draft only displacing the original once you return to the present. It isn't 100% clear from this whether other mages who are &quot;native&quot; to that draft of the past would also see only a single possible future up until the point the time-traveling mage had come from, or whether they might see multiple possible futures, reflecting the fact that the altered timeline of the draft could go in multiple different ways.<br /> <br /> 4. &quot;While still in the past, if the spell that projected the traveler backwards is dispelled, he returns to the present but any changes he made to history are reversed.&quot; So this also supports the idea that when in the past you are only altering a kind of draft of a different history, and all your changes can be undone if someone dispells your magic while you're in that draft.<br /> <br /> Could there be a way to account for all these that doesn't involve an objective present? For #1, maybe we could imagine that time has a branching structure, so that there really are multiple possible futures from any given point, but only one unique past. For the others, what if using Corridors of Time to go backwards in time created a sort of magical tether with the mage on one end and the moment/timeline they departed from on the other, such that if Corridors of Time was dispelled they would snap back to the point on the tree that they left rather than staying in the altered timeline? And this tether could also cause the temporal aura, and could determine what they see when they look into the future up to the point they departed from. Any holes in this as an alternate explanation for #2-4?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26184-jessem","name":"JesseM","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-25T23:28:13-07:00","id":1391637,"title":"","content":"I do not have access to mummy 2ed material, but i think that it must be considered that duat is a lower depth, a realm that by definition don t follow the normal metaphysical laws","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-11T20:17:59-07:00","id":1402350,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>crapcarp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1334170-spun-or-unspun-the-paradox-of-time-travel?p=1390208#post1390208\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, you necroposted on a thread that was about two-thirds of a year old and argued against points made where the material you're referencing didn't exist. To be fair, both Satchel and Arcane overreacted a bit. They have a reputation for being lore experts on these forums and don't like being contradicted. But, it's not like they were unprovoked.<br /> <br /> Thing about the CoD gamelines is that they're all designed to be their own games first; to stand on their own two feet with no other gameline supporting them. Also, CoD in general is like Burger King: you can have it your way. If you're just playing Mage and don't wanna involve any continuity from Mummy, go ahead. If you do, more power to you. Nothing's really set in stone, both in lore and mechanics (even if some people on here would have you believe otherwise). The corebooks simply give you a base and toolkit to work with.<br /> <br /> My personal take on Mage time mechanics is that time in not a wheel spinning threads, but rather a river. Like a river, Time flows in one direction, but the whole span of Time exists all at once. When a mage casts something like Shifting Sands, they pop out of the stream for a bit and thread to a previous point on the river and then dive back in. But keep in mind, this is just how I personally see it and play it. If I'm in someone else's game and they play it how the corebook does it, then I either play it that way or I simply leave the game.<br /> <br /> Please don't let this little experience drive you away from these forums. It's actually quite good here.</div> </div> </div> </div>What is a necropost? What the hell do you mean they were provoked?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26112-excess","name":"Excess","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-11T20:49:44-07:00","id":1402354,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1334170-spun-or-unspun-the-paradox-of-time-travel?p=1390196#post1390196\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What is going on, from the outside, is someone who has a demonstrable newness to the material is arguing both against the relevant newness of the material which is Mummy 2e(less than a year old) vs Mage 2nd, which was released in 2016(2015? I forget the specifics), and has, both in the final manuscript and it's follow-up supplement (2019), asserted that the way other games operate and understood their metaphysics <i>has no fucking bearing on how Mage understands it's own sense of metaphysics, and, in fact, that disparity of understanding is the fucking drive of Mage's Arcana Experience System and Mage's systems as a whole, <u>wherein Mage's work to approximate the systems of other metaphysics into the bottomless gut of their own hunger-</u></i><br /> <br /> Sorry, lost myself there-<br /> <br /> My point is that someone who has demonstrated a minimal level of experience making what is newbie level mistakes against an argument with the level of material presented, both in text and out of text, is lacking.<br /> <br /> Make up for the lack if you want people to listen.</div> </div> </div> </div>Demonstrated? Bullshit. I read the Corebook of Mage: the awakening second edition and the previews of Mummy: the curse second edition. I read signs of sorcery. I am not new to this. And so what if there is a disparity of understanding? Although meant to be internally complete so as to allow players to ignore other gamelines, they still share the same universe. The world is not a different shape for a flat-earther than it is for me, no matter our understanding. Your tantrum still doesn't make sense. You underlined the height of your tantrum and cut it off with a a hyphen as though it was an &quot;in the moment&quot; rage that you could not take back, but you apologized in the middle of a comment you could edit as many times as necessary before posting. That it still contains the tantrum with the apology demonstrates disingenuous theatrics that I will not indulge. <br /> <br /> Even if I am wrong about mage and mummy, you are still in the wrong. Obviously and absolutely in the wrong. I understand the frustration of people getting your favorite subject wrong intimately, and because I do I know that your asshole behavior does not reasonably follow. I demand you apologize, and no fauxpology either. Because in the end people are real and it is just a game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26112-excess","name":"Excess","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-11T21:15:34-07:00","id":1402360,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Excess</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1334170-spun-or-unspun-the-paradox-of-time-travel?p=1402354#post1402354\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I demand you apologize, and no fauxpology either. Because in the end people are real and it is just a game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay. Understood. 